    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39754" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pȳrămus</span></b> ,
			i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πύραμος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the lover of
			Thisbe</i>, <i>who</i>, <i>on account of
				her supposed death</i>, <i>stabbed himself under a
				mulberry-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4, 55 sq.</span></i> — Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pȳrămĕus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pyramus</i>, <i>Pyramian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbor,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the mulberry-tree</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ser. Samm. 29, 553</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
